      "itemSourceType": null,
      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": "6afb2d9c8e7aad93e9762d4d",
      "mergedPostDetails": "Noticed a regression from live regarding stations. Users in stations seem to lag behind the station, like they're returning their network position rather than being locally offset from the station.\n\nRepro steps: \n\n1. use an avatar with a seat such as this avatar:\n\nhttps://vrchat.com/home/avatar/avtr_f845b270-64e2-445b-8f9f-434aa050d05d\n\n2. Have another user get in a seat\n\n3. Move the avatar\n\n4. Observe the other user lagging behind\n\nExpectation/Behavior on Live:\n\nUser stays effectively parented/offset from the station even under  motion\n\nNotes:\n\nmainly tested this between myself and one other person who was on Live. I'll see about testing beta->beta and getting a video later.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "[1949] Users on avatar stations lag behind the station when it moves.",
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "6af28974c2db4f1c0b103ee6",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 1
      },
      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Upon further testing this seems to specifically be an issue when Live users are in a station and being viewed by a Beta user. So this likely will be 'fixed' once the beta goes live.\n\n* if the viewer and the person sitting in the station are on Live, stations behave as normal\n\n* if the viewer and the person sitting in the station are on the Beta, stations behave as normal\n\n* if a Live user sits in an avatar station then Beta viewers see them lagging behind the station. This seems to happen regardless of whether the user with the station on their avatar is on the Beta or Live. \n\nAttachment:\n\nStationBug.mp4 - A video showcasing the bug. Each side is annotated with the version the recording is on. The user wearing the avatar with a station is on the Beta. The user sitting in the station is on Live.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
